  stickyNoteInfos:
  - title: Collide Advanced
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 941
      y: -1095
      width: 711
      height: 100
    contents: type something here
    theme: Black
    textSize: Huge
  - title: 'Animated Noise position:'
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: -541
      y: -421
      width: 323
      height: 177
    contents: 'An animated spawn position can add interesting motion to a particle
      simulation.

      In this example, we are using the VFX time as a coordinate
      to sample a value noise 3D.

      It results in an animated offset that we
      are adding to a position operator, which is the ''base'' position, and that
      can be tweaked in the scene.



      The initial position of our circle is
      derived from this animated noise.

'
    theme: Black
    textSize: Small
  - title: 'Random Mass:'
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 1402
      y: -9
      width: 217
      height: 100
    contents: 'Mass affects how particles react to force. Randomization of mass is
      a good way to add some variation to the particle''s motion and behavior.

'
    theme: Black
    textSize: Small
  - title: 'Collide with SDF:'
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: -212
      y: 1049
      width: 562
      height: 368
    contents: 'We''re providing an SDF to the distance field settings, and we''re
      giving the size and position that we''re given by the SDF baker tool.



      This
      "collide with SDF" block lets our particles collide with an SDF.

      The
      particles in this case collide with the SDF representation of the hand mesh.

      The
      SDF is rotating in sync with the hand''s mesh.

'
    theme: Black
    textSize: Medium
  - title: 'Colide With Cone:'
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 1402
      y: 1369
      width: 447
      height: 181
    contents: 'This secondary collide block will cause the particles to collide with
      a cone shape similar to a mount of sand. '
    theme: Black
    textSize: Medium
  - title: 'Colide With Cone:'
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 507
      y: 1629
      width: 447
      height: 177
    contents: 'The third collision block is designed to ensure that the sand particles
      collide with the statue pedestal. '
    theme: Black
    textSize: Medium
  - title: 'Animated Turbulence Transform:'
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: 1397
      y: 746
      width: 342
      height: 104
    contents: "The \u201Cturbulence force\u201D block makes our particles move in
      interesting organic ways.\r\nWe can get even more appealing and fluid motions
      by animating the transform.\r\n"
    theme: Black
    textSize: Small
  - title: Velocity Noise Variation
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: -954
      y: 747
      width: 350
      height: 100
    contents: Some velocity variation is created by sampling a Perlin noise. We take
      the velocity.Y absolute value and multiply it by -1 so that the velocity vector
      variation is always going downward.
    theme: Black
    textSize: Small
  - title: Hand Mesh
    position:
      serializedVersion: 2
      x: -809
      y: 2221
      width: 493
      height: 100
    contents: type something here
    theme: Black
    textSize: Huge
  categories: []
  uiBounds:
    serializedVersion: 2
    x: -954
    y: -1095
    width: 3818
    height: 4059
